UyNTZlMmQ4NTAyMDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/JNZader/portfolio-2025/commit/22c47f0ad1b55ba25f9dda038f104db7c6b908ec","sha":"22c47f0ad1b55ba25f9dda038f104db7c6b908ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JNZader/portfolio-2025/commits/22c47f0ad1b55ba25f9dda038f104db7c6b908ec"}],"sha":"1da2979df76c762664b18966c9c5256e2d850200","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JNZader/portfolio-2025/commits/1da2979df76c762664b18966c9c5256e2d850200"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127463636?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JNZader/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JNZader/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JNZader/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JNZader/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JNZader","id":127463636,"login":"JNZader","node_id":"U_kgDOB5jw1A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JNZader/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JNZader/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JNZader/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JNZader/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JNZader/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JNZader","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JNZader/portfolio-2025/commits/22c47f0ad1b55ba25f9dda038f104db7c6b908ec/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T00:13:50Z","email":"127463636+JNZader@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Javier Zader"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T00:13:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(qa): cite published case studies without sending the thread (#275)\n\n* feat(qa): add grounded corpus matcher for published apps\n\nAssemble per-locale chunks from case-study prose and CV education.\nRefuse weak queries. Drop origin READMEs when a case study has a body.\n\nVerified: npx vitest run __tests__/unit/qa/corpus.test.ts — 12/12 passed.\n\n* feat(qa): snapshot published corpus at build time\n\nLoad es/en chunks from local case studies and resume JSON.\nPublic READMEs stay caller-supplied and never come from GitHub.\n\nVerified: ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run __tests__/unit/qa/ — 17/17 passed.\n\n* feat(qa): add POST /api/qa on the api-mutation bucket\n\nQuote published snapshot chunks with CSRF and body validation.\nReuse the proxy mutation bucket; do not add a Redis limiter.\n\nVerified: ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run __tests__/unit/api\n__tests__/unit/rate-limit/rate-limit-policy.test.ts __tests__/unit/qa\n— 95/95 passed.\n\n* feat(qa): add published Q&A input on /proyectos\n\nSingle-turn form posts to /api/qa and shows a citation link.\nCatalogues cover es and en. Playwright stays environment-blocked.\n\nVerified: ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run\n__tests__/integration/components/PublishedQaForm.test.tsx — 7/7 passed.\n\n* feat(qa): ground /proyectos chat on Gemini Flash\n\nRetrieve published chunks, stream only when evidence exists, and\nskip Google when retrieval is empty. Chat UI replaces the quote form.\n\nVerified: ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run __tests__/unit/qa\n__tests__/unit/api/qa-route.test.ts\n__tests__/integration/components/PublishedQaForm.test.tsx — 41/41 passed.\n\n* fix(qa): use gemini-3.8-flash for new Google keys\n\ngemini-2.5-flash rejects new users; the stream then surfaced a generic\nclient error. Point the route at the replacement Flash id.\n\nVerified: ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run __tests__/unit/api/qa-route.test.ts\n— 10/10 passed. Live POST /api/qa returned a UI stream without errorText.\n\n* fix(qa): strip Gemini thought signatures from the chat stream\n\nNew Flash keys attach a thoughtSignature to an empty text-delta.\nThe browser then marks useChat as error after a long 200 response.\n\nVerified: ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run __tests__/unit/api/qa-route.test.ts\n— 10/10 passed. Live stream has no thoughtSignature or empty deltas.\n\n* fix(qa): keep SSE framing and assign chat message ids\n\nDropping blank SSE lines broke the browser parser after a long 200.\nMissing generateMessageId left the assistant stream unrendered.\n\nVerified: qa-route tests 10/10. Playwright on /proyectos showed the\nAPiGen Java answer in the chat log with no catalog error.\n\n* feat(qa): float a site-wide chat that prefers the current page\n\nOpen a panel from any locale route. Retrieval boosts the project or\nblog slug in the URL. Back-to-top moves left so it does not cover it.\n\nVerified: ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run __tests__/unit/qa\n__tests__/unit/api/qa-route.test.ts\n__tests__/integration/components/PublishedQaForm.test.tsx — 53/53 passed.\n\n* fix(qa): cap Gemini per IP and drop chat history to the model\n\nDedicated 10/10m limiter before retrieve. The model sees one quoted\nQUESTION plus SOURCES, not prior turns, so it cannot be steered off\nthe published corpus.\n\nVerified: ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run __tests__/unit/api/qa-route.test.ts\n— 16/16 passed.\n\n* docs: draft blog post on the published chat pipeline\n\nSanity-ready markdown: corpus, retrieval, Gemini, rate limits, and\nwhat the chat will not do. Blog posts are not in the snapshot yet.\n\nVerified: N/A — documentation only.\n\n* feat(qa): polish chat log with typing, JZ label, and lists\n\nAuto-scroll the transcript, show a writing state, and render\nmarkdown lists in assistant bubbles without changing the FAB.\n\nVerified: ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run\n__tests__/integration/components/PublishedQaForm.test.tsx — 13/13 passed.\n\n* feat(qa): answer greetings without calling Gemini\n\nhola and similar greeting-only lines get a canned welcome. Off-topic\nquestions still refuse. Google is not invoked.\n\nVerified: ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run __tests__/unit/qa\n__tests__/unit/api/qa-route.test.ts\n__tests__/integration/components/PublishedQaForm.test.tsx — 81/81 passed.\n\n* docs(qa): rewrite the published chat post\n\nWalk three questions through the request path, the lexical floor, and\nthe two Redis ceilings that actually apply to POST /api/qa.\n\n* fix(about): keep the contact CV control at content width\n\nfullWidth stretched the split button across the about column below the\nlg breakpoint, so the download half sat in an empty bar.\n\n* test(qa): accept forwarded args in route mocks\n\ntsc rejected the zero-arg vi.fn wrappers when the mock factories\nspread the real call arguments.\n\n* test(qa): compare README citations exactly\n\nCodeQL treats includes(''github.com'') as an incomplete URL check. The\nBiogas corpus test now rejects the full README citation.","tree":{"sha":"68b5ec3b3620b03451419306615ea9ec529be23f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JNZader/portfolio-2025/git/trees/68b5ec3b3620b03451419306615ea9ec529be23f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JNZader/portfolio-2025/git/commits/22c47f0ad1b55ba25f9dda038f104db7c6b908ec","verification":{"payload":"tree 68b5ec3b3620b03451419306615ea9ec529be23f\nparent e0bcecf088eba4bc8c764e7c0033c3d8e36f42a1\nauthor Javier Zader <127463636+JNZader@users.noreply.github.com> 1790468030 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790468030 -0300\n\nfeat(qa): cite published case studies without sending the thread (#275)\n\n* feat(qa): add grounded corpus matcher for published apps\n\nAssemble per-locale chunks from case-study prose and CV education.\nRefuse weak queries. Drop origin READMEs when a case study has a body.\n\nVerified: npx vitest run __tests__/unit/qa/corpus.test.ts — 12/12 passed.\n\n* feat(qa): snapshot published corpus at build time\n\nLoad es/en chunks from local case studies and resume JSON.\nPublic READMEs stay caller-supplied and never come from GitHub.\n\nVerified: ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run __tests__/unit/qa/ — 17/17 passed.\n\n* feat(qa): add POST /api/qa on the api-mutation bucket\n\nQuote published snapshot chunks with CSRF and body validation.\nReuse the proxy mutation bucket; do not add a Redis limiter.\n\nVerified: ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run __tests__/unit/api\n__tests__/unit/rate-limit/rate-limit-policy.test.ts __tests__/unit/qa\n— 95/95 passed.\n\n* feat(qa): add published Q&A input on /proyectos\n\nSingle-turn form posts to /api/qa and shows a citation link.\nCatalogues cover es and en. Playwright stays environment-blocked.\n\nVerified: ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run\n__tests__/integration/components/PublishedQaForm.test.tsx — 7/7 passed.\n\n* feat(qa): ground /proyectos chat on Gemini Flash\n\nRetrieve published chunks, stream only when evidence exists, and\nskip Google when retrieval is empty. Chat UI replaces the quote form.\n\nVerified: ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run __tests__/unit/qa\n__tests__/unit/api/qa-route.test.ts\n__tests__/integration/components/PublishedQaForm.test.tsx — 41/41 passed.\n\n* fix(qa): use gemini-3.8-flash for new Google keys\n\ngemini-2.5-flash rejects new users; the stream then surfaced a generic\nclient error. Point the route at the replacement Flash id.\n\nVerified: ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run __tests__/unit/api/qa-route.test.ts\n— 10/10 passed. Live POST /api/qa returned a UI stream without errorText.\n\n* fix(qa): strip Gemini thought signatures from the chat stream\n\nNew Flash keys attach a thoughtSignature to an empty text-delta.\nThe browser then marks useChat as error after a long 200 response.\n\nVerified: ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run __tests__/unit/api/qa-route.test.ts\n— 10/10 passed. Live stream has no thoughtSignature or empty deltas.\n\n* fix(qa): keep SSE framing and assign chat message ids\n\nDropping blank SSE lines broke the browser parser after a long 200.\nMissing generateMessageId left the assistant stream unrendered.\n\nVerified: qa-route tests 10/10. Playwright on /proyectos showed the\nAPiGen Java answer in the chat log with no catalog error.\n\n* feat(qa): float a site-wide chat that prefers the current page\n\nOpen a panel from any locale route.