ist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dt2patel","id":60128132,"login":"dt2patel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMTI4MTMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt2patel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt2patel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt2patel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt2patel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt2patel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt2patel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hotwax/accxui/commits/2565489b5e6f9652e51ecbf848e7a0108ec83c2f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T17:36:33Z","email":"heyadityapatel@gmail.com","name":"Aditya Patel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T17:36:33Z","email":"heyadityapatel@gmail.com","name":"Aditya Patel"},"message":"Fixed: Kept the schema version when logout clears the app database, so the next login does not rebuild it\n\nclearDatabaseTables also emptied syncMeta, removing the schemaVersion record. The main thread had already checked the version in this realm, so after a logout and login in the same tab it wrote straight to the database. The sync worker the login started is a realm of its own: it found no record, took the database for an unrecorded build, and deleted and rebuilt it, dropping what the main thread had written. In fulfillment that is the facility master list, so the Open page stayed empty until a reload. Logout now deletes every syncMeta row except schemaVersion.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"14fd00e5c2e774cb37756aaf6f30b12a54fb86fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hotwax/accxui/git/trees/14fd00e5c2e774cb37756aaf6f30b12a54fb86fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hotwax/accxui/git/commits/2565489b5e6f9652e51ecbf848e7a0108ec83c2f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60128132?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt2patel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt2patel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt2patel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt2patel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dt2patel","id":60128132,"login":"dt2patel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMTI4MTMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt2patel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt2patel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt2patel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt2patel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt2patel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt2patel","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/hotwax/accxui/commit/2565489b5e6f9652e51ecbf848e7a0108ec83c2f","node_id":"C_kwDOQQ6FmNoAKDI1NjU0ODliNWU2Zjk2NTJlNTFlY2JmODQ4ZTdhMDEwOGVjODNjMmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/hotwax/accxui/commit/c91b85dbcbcc74fad454a38bf64615a2ff30ad9c","sha":"c91b85dbcbcc74fad454a38bf64615a2ff30ad9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hotwax/accxui/commits/c91b85dbcbcc74fad454a38bf64615a2ff30ad9c"}],"sha":"2565489b5e6f9652e51ecbf848e7a0108ec83c2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hotwax/accxui/commits/2565489b5e6f9652e51ecbf848e7a0108ec83c2f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60128132?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt2patel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt2patel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt2patel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt2patel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dt2patel","id":60128132,"login":"dt2patel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMTI4MTMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt2patel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt2patel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt2patel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt2patel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt2patel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt2patel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hotwax/accxui/commits/77a827e1db91434854ec98a084abf4a46b0b119a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T15:37:02Z","email":"heyadityapatel@gmail.com","name":"Aditya Patel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T15:37:02Z","email":"heyadityapatel@gmail.com","name":"Aditya Patel"},"message":"Fixed: database version check failing when a live query opens the database first\n\nensureDbReady''s first-use version check writes the schema marker, and on a\nmismatch rebuilds the database. Live queries reach it from inside their\nquerier (dbClient.live, useSeedData, useDbStatus), where Dexie refuses\nwrites, so when a live query was the first use the check failed with\nReadOnlyError, the marker was never written, and the database was rebuilt\non every load. Dexie also echoes a live query''s zone into native\ncontinuations, so a check started by another caller could be refused the\nsame way, and that caller could resume inside the live query, where its\nown later writes failed. A querier that awaited a check another caller had\nstarted resumed outside its live query instead, so its reads were not\ntracked and it never re-ran.\n\nThe open and the check now run in Dexie''s global zone as a chain of Dexie\npromises, and ensureDbReady returns a Dexie promise made in its caller''s\nzone: a querier resumes inside its live query, and any other caller\nresumes outside it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 