\nthe repo rather than in a terminal scrollback: the three failing checks and\nthe lint crash as they were on feat/agent, and the same commands on this\nbranch.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"11abb598098bf525f44292879ed7fb0ef89124db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/git/trees/11abb598098bf525f44292879ed7fb0ef89124db"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/git/commits/8e52d12c36654dc3760938f1270e288f7a30a6ee","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/155999523?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aditya-deokar","id":155999523,"login":"aditya-deokar","node_id":"U_kgDOCUxdIw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aditya-deokar/a8n/commit/8e52d12c36654dc3760938f1270e288f7a30a6ee","node_id":"C_kwDOQRy4s9oAKDhlNTJkMTJjMzY2NTRkYzM3NjA5MzhmMTI3MGUyODhmN2EzMGE2ZWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aditya-deokar/a8n/commit/39b2cf5ebe157a55e291e8560db25e9684e665d5","sha":"39b2cf5ebe157a55e291e8560db25e9684e665d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/commits/39b2cf5ebe157a55e291e8560db25e9684e665d5"}],"sha":"8e52d12c36654dc3760938f1270e288f7a30a6ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/commits/8e52d12c36654dc3760938f1270e288f7a30a6ee"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/155999523?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aditya-deokar","id":155999523,"login":"aditya-deokar","node_id":"U_kgDOCUxdIw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/commits/39b2cf5ebe157a55e291e8560db25e9684e665d5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T14:54:05Z","email":"adityadeokar80@gmail.com","name":"adiya-deokar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T14:54:05Z","email":"adityadeokar80@gmail.com","name":"adiya-deokar"},"message":"test(mcp): audit the runtime surface and unblock the eval chain\n\nmcp:contract:check works by grepping source, so it cannot see what the server\nregisters at runtime. mcp:runtime:audit boots the real McpServer for each app\nprofile and checks what is actually there: tool and resource counts, that\nevery widget tool points at a resource that exists, that annotations reached\nthe tools, and that model-facing docs name only registered tools. It runs in\nmcp:release:gate.\n\nThree gates were red before this:\n\n- mcp:contract:check and mcp:safety:check both asserted a hard-coded\n  `=== 28` ChatGPT tool count. The set was consolidated to 26 and the\n  literals never followed, so both failed on a tool set that was correct.\n  They derive the count from the contract now.\n- mcp:continuous:check failed because the dashboard had no security center,\n  which was true.\n\ntest:mcp:offline chains four scripts with &&, and it failed at the second, so\nthe ChatGPT app eval and the adversarial eval never ran. Both were also\nbroken: one expected get_integration_setup_guide and the other targeted\nexecute_workflow, tools removed during consolidation. All four suites pass.\n\nThe same consolidation left a8n://docs/api, the prompt contracts, the\nsubmission assets and two prompts instructing the model to call\nexecute_workflow, get_integration_setup_guide, test_webhook_setup and\nget_webhook_url — none of which exist. A client reading those resources would\nattempt failing tool calls. The runtime audit now fails if a model-facing\nfile names an unregistered tool.\n\ntsconfig.scripts.json maps server-only to the existing test stub so a script\ncan boot the app graph under tsx.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6b514000787f8a1322d2bc82ea451653ecf4cc61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/git/trees/6b514000787f8a1322d2bc82ea451653ecf4cc61"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/git/commits/39b2cf5ebe157a55e291e8560db25e9684e665d5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/155999523?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aditya-deokar","id":155999523,"login":"aditya-deokar","node_id":"U_kgDOCUxdIw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aditya-deokar/a8n/commit/39b2cf5ebe157a55e291e8560db25e9684e665d5","node_id":"C_kwDOQRy4s9oAKDM5YjJjZjVlYmUxNTdhNTVlMjkxZTg1NjBkYjI1ZTk2ODRlNjY1ZDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aditya-deokar/a8n/commit/8f512f34474825cb9dfd54f3952b6b1ee509cb80","sha":"8f512f34474825cb9dfd54f3952b6b1ee509cb80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/commits/8f512f34474825cb9dfd54f3952b6b1ee509cb80"}],"sha":"39b2cf5ebe157a55e291e8560db25e9684e665d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/commits/39b2cf5ebe157a55e291e8560db25e9684e665d5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/155999523?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aditya-deokar","id":155999523,"login":"aditya-deokar","node_id":"U_kgDOCUxdIw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/commits/8f512f34474825cb9dfd54f3952b6b1ee509cb80/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T14:53:52Z","email":"adityadeokar80@gmail.com","name":"adiya-deokar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T14:53:52Z","email":"adityadeokar80@gmail.com","name":"adiya-deokar"},"message":"fix(mcp-ui): mount the security center and fix the dashboard''s a11y gaps\n\nMcpSecurityCenter was written, exported and never rendered. The /mcp page\nstill prefetched securitySummary on every load, so the most expensive query\non the page ran for a component that did not exist — and the component threw\naway data.recommendations, the only actionable part of the payload. It is now\nmounted, renders the recommendations, and no longer duplicates the OAuth\nconnection list that McpOAuthConnections already owns.\n\nThe client integration snippets could not be pasted anywhere: several\nconcatenated two JSON objects with a // comment between them, which is not\nvalid JSON. Each preset is now a single valid artifact, with Claude Code''s\nnative `claude mcp add` command, a VS Code preset, and the extra variants\nmoved to notes beside the snippet.\n\nAccessibility:\n- scope rows were clickable divs wrapping a Checkbox with no change handler,\n  so the whole permission picker was unreachable by keyboard; they are labels\n  with real checkboxes now\n- icon-only close and copy buttons had no accessible name\n- the slide-over had no dialog role and no way to dismiss it from the\n  keyboard; Escape closes it and focus moves into it\n- a failed OAuth connections query fell through to the empty state and told\n  the user they had no connected clients\n- clipboard writes are guarded: navigator.clipboard is unavailable over plain\n  HTTP, and both call sites failed silently\n- w-[400px] with no max-width overflowed narrow viewports; py-0.2 was not a\n  real Tailwind token so that padding never applied\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e54095ca63f06c8c98d1c04d646a78b6ebb7491d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/git/trees/e54095ca63f06c8c98d1c04d646a78b6ebb7491d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/git/commits/8f512f34474825cb9dfd54f3952b6b1ee509cb80","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/155999523?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aditya-deokar","id":155999523,"login":"aditya-deokar","node_id":"U_kgDOCUxdIw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aditya-deokar/a8n/commit/8f512f34474825cb9dfd54f3952b6b1ee509cb80","node_id":"C_kwDOQRy4s9oAKDhmNTEyZjM0NDc0ODI1Y2I5ZGZkNTRmMzk1MmI2YjFlZTUwOWNiODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aditya-deokar/a8n/commit/f66c10fd167aa750a7c62ff0ae5d155d1231a8be","sha":"f66c10fd167aa750a7c62ff0ae5d155d1231a8be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/commits/f66c10fd167aa750a7c62ff0ae5d155d1231a8be"}],"sha":"8f512f34474825cb9dfd54f3952b6b1ee509cb80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/commits/8f512f34474825cb9dfd54f3952b6b1ee509cb80"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/155999523?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aditya-deokar","id":155999523,"login":"aditya-deokar","node_id":"U_kgDOCUxdIw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/commits/f66c10fd167aa750a7c62ff0ae5d155d1231a8be/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T14:53:39Z","email":"adityadeokar80@gmail.com","name":"adiya-deokar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T14:53:39Z","email":"adityadeokar80@gmail.com","name":"adiya-deokar"},"message":"fix(mcp-apps): make the widgets work, and look like they belong\n\nEvery widget captured the connected app from initWidget(...).then(...), but\nthe render callback can fire from ontoolresult before that promise resolves.\nWhen it did, the widget rendered with a null app, every action button stayed\ndisabled, and nothing re-rendered to fix it — so \"Apply this draft\" and\n\"Diagnose this failure\" were permanently dead. The bridge now keeps the last\npayload, re-renders when the connection arrives, and hands the app to the\nrender callback.\n\nCHATGPT_WIDGET_CSP was exported, advertised in the resource metadata and\nasserted by a test, but nothing ever put it in the HTML: every built widget\nshipped with no CSP. The build now injects it.\n\nHosts set the theme with data-theme on <html>, which the stylesheet ignored\nin favour of prefers-color-scheme, so a dark host on a light machine rendered\na light widget. Both paths are handled now.\n\nAlso:\n- the setup checklist no longer fires a google_form test for workflows with\n  no webhook trigger, and sends one test per distinct trigger\n- the redactor only matches assignment-shaped secrets; it was rewriting\n  \"shared-secret verification\" into \"shared-secret [REDACTED]\"\n- widgets get skeleton, empty, disconnected and error states instead of a\n  bare \"Waiting for widget data\" panel\n- the approval widget says why an invalid draft cannot be applied rather than\n  showing a disabled button with no explanation\n\nThe e2e suite asserted against a window.openai shim the widgets stopped using\nwhen they moved to the ext-apps SDK, so it was testing nothing — and its CSP\nassertion could never have passed. tests/e2e/mcp/host-harness.ts implements a\nreal MCP Apps host, and the suite now drives the widgets the way a host does:\n78 tests covering render, interaction, escaping, redaction, CSP, phone width\nand both themes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b239c97f61c65880e3fe27edff56a78635341f83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/git/trees/b239c97f61c65880e3fe27edff56a78635341f83"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/git/commits/f66c10fd167aa750a7c62ff0ae5d155d1231a8be","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/155999523?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aditya-deokar","id":155999523,"login":"aditya-deokar","node_id":"U_kgDOCUxdIw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aditya-deokar/a8n/commit/f66c10fd167aa750a7c62ff0ae5d155d1231a8be","node_id":"C_kwDOQRy4s9oAKGY2NmMxMGZkMTY3YWE3NTBhN2M2MmZmMGFlNWQxNTVkMTIzMWE4YmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aditya-deokar/a8n/commit/f82ac311daae438c07dbc3a2be28a482af1b416a","sha":"f82ac311daae438c07dbc3a2be28a482af1b416a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/commits/f82ac311daae438c07dbc3a2be28a482af1b416a"}],"sha":"f66c10fd167aa750a7c62ff0ae5d155d1231a8be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/commits/f66c10fd167aa750a7c62ff0ae5d155d1231a8be"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/155999523?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aditya-deokar","id":155999523,"login":"aditya-deokar","node_id":"U_kgDOCUxdIw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/commits/f82ac311daae438c07dbc3a2be28a482af1b416a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T14:53:24Z","email":"adityadeokar80@gmail.com","name":"adiya-deokar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T14:53:24Z","email":"adityadeokar80@gmail.com","name":"adiya-deokar"},"message":"fix(mcp): make the server behave correctly for non-ChatGPT clients\n\nGET /api/mcp built a full server and returned a 200 SSE stream that nothing\ncould write to and nothing closed. The SDK client opens exactly that stream\nafter initialize and only treats 405 as \"no server-initiated stream\", so\nevery SDK-based client held a connection that never emitted — and on\nserverless it pinned a function open until it was killed. GET now answers\n405 with an Allow header, and DELETE stops building a 52-tool server to\nperform a no-op.\n\nThe contract manifest declares readOnlyHint/destructiveHint for every tool,\nbut 45 of 52 register through an SDK overload with no annotations parameter,\nso no client ever saw them: list_workflows looked exactly as risky as\ndelete_workflow to a host deciding whether to prompt for confirmation.\napplyContractAnnotations copies the hints onto registered tools, leaving\ntools that set their own alone.\n\nAlso:\n- declare the logging capability; without it logging/setLevel answers -32601\n  and MCP Inspector''s log-level control fails\n- expose WWW-Authenticate, which is not CORS-safelisted, so browser clients\n  can read resource_metadata off a 401\n- serve /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/api/mcp, which RFC 9728 clients\n  probe before falling back to the root document\n- drop the oninitialized hook: under the stateless transport it can never see\n  client capabilities, and had it run it would have thrown \"already\n  registered\" inside a notification handler where the SDK swallows errors\n- default MCP_CORS_ORIGINS to the app origin; the wildcard default turned an\n  unset env var into a 500 on every request in production\n\nThe wildcard refusal deliberately still returns no CORS headers. An earlier\nversion of this change relaxed that and the repo''s own test caught it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2c4f9e9cb8a2b4b075bfe23175a14d3499c1edd3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/git/trees/2c4f9e9cb8a2b4b075bfe23175a14d3499c1edd3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/git/commits/f82ac311daae438c07dbc3a2be28a482af1b416a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/155999523?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aditya-deokar","id":155999523,"login":"aditya-deokar","node_id":"U_kgDOCUxdIw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aditya-deokar/a8n/commit/f82ac311daae438c07dbc3a2be28a482af1b416a","node_id":"C_kwDOQRy4s9oAKGY4MmFjMzExZGFhZTQzOGMwN2RiYzNhMmJlMjhhNDgyYWYxYjQxNmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aditya-deokar/a8n/commit/7f8f045fca3acb69a7126fa077c3bfdd7cc8515b","sha":"7f8f045fca3acb69a7126fa077c3bfdd7cc8515b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/commits/7f8f045fca3acb69a7126fa077c3bfdd7cc8515b"}],"sha":"f82ac311daae438c07dbc3a2be28a482af1b416a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/commits/f82ac311daae438c07dbc3a2be28a482af1b416a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/155999523?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aditya-deokar","id":155999523,"login":"aditya-deokar","node_id":"U_kgDOCUxdIw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/commits/7f8f045fca3acb69a7126fa077c3bfdd7cc8515b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T14:53:11Z","email":"adityadeokar80@gmail.com","name":"adiya-deokar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T14:53:11Z","email":"adityadeokar80@gmail.com","name":"adiya-deokar"},"message":"perf(mcp): remove N+1 and add the missing access-path indexes\n\nThe MCP surface read through unindexed foreign keys. Postgres does not\nindex them automatically, so every workflow graph load, graph rewrite and\ncascade delete sequentially scanned Node, Connection and Execution — and\nNode had no indexes at all.\n\nAdds the missing indexes and drops four that duplicated an existing UNIQUE\nconstraint, costing writes on tables touched by every MCP request.\n\nlistMcpOAuthConnectionsForUser issued four queries per connected client and\nthe /mcp page called it twice per load: 88 statements per page load with ten\nconnected clients, now 16 and constant, via groupBy.\n\nAlso:\n- list_executions selects explicit columns instead of pulling `output` (a\n  full execution payload) and `errorStack` for every row\n- lastUsedAt writes are throttled to 60s, removing an UPDATE and a WAL write\n  from every authenticated request on both the API-key and OAuth paths\n- move_workflow_node updates one row instead of deleting and recreating the\n  whole graph to change a node position\n- getMcpAuditHealth counts a bounded window instead of the whole audit table\n\nMeasured on a seeded local Postgres, median of three runs: 18.4ms -> 9.7ms\nacross the benchmarked queries, sequential scans 5 -> 2. Two sub-millisecond\nOAuth queries moved within noise and are reported as such. Raw EXPLAIN output\nand the reproduction steps are in docs/mcp/evidence/db-optimization/.\n\nThe migration is hand-written so it carries only these index changes; a\ngenerated one would also have dropped agent_memory_item, which is unrelated\npre-existing drift.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"52ca1b27b29e70da8b3c743bc0164f8ca08d594f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/git/trees/52ca1b27b29e70da8b3c743bc0164f8ca08d594f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/git/commits/7f8f045fca3acb69a7126fa077c3bfdd7cc8515b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/155999523?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aditya-deokar","id":155999523,"login":"aditya-deokar","node_id":"U_kgDOCUxdIw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aditya-deokar/a8n/commit/7f8f045fca3acb69a7126fa077c3bfdd7cc8515b","node_id":"C_kwDOQRy4s9oAKDdmOGYwNDVmY2EzYWNiNjlhNzEyNmZhMDc3YzNiZmRkN2NjODUxNWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aditya-deokar/a8n/commit/cbfe43322965019e30e8e54c482be9379c554610","sha":"cbfe43322965019e30e8e54c482be9379c554610","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/commits/cbfe43322965019e30e8e54c482be9379c554610"}],"sha":"7f8f045fca3acb69a7126fa077c3bfdd7cc8515b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/commits/7f8f045fca3acb69a7126fa077c3bfdd7cc8515b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/155999523?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/events{/privacy}","follower