gmail.com","name":"adiya-deokar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T18:08:22Z","email":"adityadeokar80@gmail.com","name":"adiya-deokar"},"message":"feat(subscription): freemium quota system with Polar sync\n\nShip the Free tier (5 workflows, 10 credentials, 25 agent chats/month)\nand meter everything server-side with race-safe quota enforcement.\n\nCore:\n- Local entitlement mirror (Subscription) synced from Polar via signed\n  webhooks + daily reconciliation cron; plan resolver honors period-end\n- Race-safe stock quotas (pg advisory lock tx) and flow meters\n  (conditional UPDATE counters, calendar-month windows)\n- Enforcement: workflows.create / credentials.create / chat SSE 402 /\n  MCP shared guard (+ real tier into MCP rate limiter) / daily\n  execution abuse guard wired into dispatch\n- Agent runs now persist token usage and enforce per-run cost budget\n- Config-driven Polar server/product IDs; production env fail-fast\n\nBilling sync:\n- POST /api/webhooks/polar (Standard Webhooks verify, dedup ledger,\n  stale-event skip, unlinked-customer alerts)\n- subscriptions.syncNow (rate-limited) + getSnapshot for UI meters\n- Reconciliation drift repair where Polar wins; counter cross-check vs\n  immutable AgentRun ledger; GC hooked into maintenance cron\n- Idempotent backfill script; checkout-return entitlement sync UI\n\nUX:\n- Sidebar usage meters + grandfathered over-limit banner\n- Contextual upgrade modal from QUOTA_EXCEEDED payloads (tRPC\n  errorFormatter wire contract)\n- Composer 402 banner with reset chip and upgrade CTA\n- Pricing page truth-aligned to shipped v1 features\n\nOps:\n- Migration 20260822120000_subscription_quota_models (additive only)\n- Fault injection: polar-webhook, quota-db; observability events\n  billing.quota.denied/consume + billing.webhook.*\n- Production deploy workflow: inject POLAR_SERVER/PRO_PRODUCT_ID/\n  WEBHOOK_SECRET/BILLING_RECONCILE_SECRET/ENTITLEMENTS_ENABLED\n- Tests: unit + integration suites incl. live-PG race suite\n  (quota-race.db.test.mjs) that caught void-lock deserialization,\n  upsert unique-race, and pool self-deadlock bugs\n- Docs: docs/subscription/* (model, architecture, security,\n  testing, rollout, decisions D1-D8, support macros)","tree":{"sha":"364feab37f1570949c41e0da5f7e77e8f3ec2e08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/git/trees/364feab37f1570949c41e0da5f7e77e8f3ec2e08"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aditya-deokar/a8n/git/commits/f8082c10256e922f85b7e7f21941a01107337c9a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/155999523?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aditya-deokar","id":155999523,"login":"aditya-deokar","node_id":"U_kgDOCUxdIw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aditya-deokar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aditya-deokar/a8n/commit/f8082c10256e922f85b7e7f21941a01107337c9a","node_id":"C_kwDOQRy4s9oAKGY4MDgyYzEwMjU2ZTkyMmY4NWI3ZTdmMjE5NDFhMDExMDczMzdjOWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aditya-deokar/a8n/commit/163c227d2861ab47ff52817507a8b95ddfb71bb8","sha":"163c227d2861ab47ff52817507a8b95ddfb71bb8","url":"https://api.github.com/rep